{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalDqSquared","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalDqSquared","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.GroupWithZero.Units.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.dq_squared_nonzero_generic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.dq_squared_nonzero_generic","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-dq-squared.lean#L106-L112","doc":"For q ≠ 1, dq² ≠ 0 on generic (non-Reeb-invariant) forms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.dq_squared_zero_on_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.dq_squared_zero_on_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-dq-squared.lean#L99-L104","doc":"On Reeb-invariant forms, dq is a cochain differential (dq² = 0). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.categorical_dq_squared","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.categorical_dq_squared","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-dq-squared.lean#L88-L97","doc":"**Non-vanishing of dq²** (categorical statement of `prop:categorical-dq-squared`).\n\n`dq² = 0 ⟺ q = 1 ∨ [ξ, α] = 0` — equivalently, for `q ≠ 1` the\nobstruction is nonzero on any non-Reeb-invariant form, so the\nq-deformed de Rham complex is *not* a cochain complex. This is the\ndecl named by the content block's `lean.ref`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:categorical-dq-squared","label":"prop:categorical-dq-squared","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-dq-squared.md"},{"@id":"block:prf:categorical-dq-squared","label":"prf:categorical-dq-squared","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-dq-squared-proof.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.dq_squared_vanishes_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.dq_squared_vanishes_iff","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-dq-squared.lean#L67-L86","doc":"dq² vanishes iff q = 1 or the form is Reeb-invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DqSquaredObstruction.obstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DqSquaredObstruction.obstruction","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-dq-squared.lean#L60-L65","doc":"The dq² obstruction: `dq²(α) = q⁻¹(1 - q⁻¹) · [ξ, α]`.\nDefined as a function of the data so the vanishing theorems below are\nnon-vacuous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DqSquaredObstruction.reeb_bracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DqSquaredObstruction.reeb_bracket","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-dq-squared.lean#L56-L56","doc":"The Reeb-bracket value [ξ, α] (scalar representative). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DqSquaredObstruction.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DqSquaredObstruction.q","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-dq-squared.lean#L54-L54","doc":"The substrate parameter q, carried as a unit — algebraic\ninvertibility (the old `q ≠ 0`), not the archimedean `0 < q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DqSquaredObstruction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DqSquaredObstruction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-dq-squared.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.DqSquaredObstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.DqSquaredObstruction","kind":"structure","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-dq-squared.lean#L48-L56","doc":"**dq² obstruction data**: the substrate `q` (as a unit of the ground\nring) and the Reeb-bracket value `[ξ, α]`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}